				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/duganist" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7085155); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7085155&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606937946" alt="Duganist" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7085155)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/duganist" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7085155); return false;" >Duganist</a></span> <span class="odate time_1606937941 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">02 Dec 2020 19:39</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-50742/per-page-discussions">Per Page Discussions / Per page discussions</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/scp-5923/comments/show">SCP-5923</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4834605">
									

<p>This is the second article I wrote after The 13 Correlation, which I'll admit suffers from some first-article frays. This has memetic infiltration, pro career cover-ups, cosmic invasion/apocalypse catalyst, auto-creation of reality through observer effects, a play by play of a rapid Big Rip in the Foundation-verse, how it'd interact with various physical anomalies, a precision redaction about one of my favorite early SCPs that seems creepy in a mystical way.</p>
<p>And to top it off, a spook. I didn't expect to find a face in a quasar.</p>
<p>I think I'm hitting a lot of SCP-genre keynotes here while also bringing some fresh spin. I hope you agree.</p>

