<p>Here are a few suggestions:</p>
<ul>
<li>&quot;SCP-3178 is seasoning which consists of the composition normally found in factory-made monosodium glutamate with the addition of an unidentified substance.&quot; -&gt; &quot;SCP-3178 is a seasoning consisting of factory-made monosodium glutamate and an unidentified substance.&quot; It's a minor prose nitpick, but excessive prepositional phrases hurt your clarity and conciseness. I have the same problem, and recommend running your writing through Slickwrite.com to catch it.</li>
<li>&quot;the balanced flavour of SCP-3178&quot; is a bit too subjective for my liking. Also, the author can't really know that unless they also tasted it. Maybe say that subjects report the flavor as balanced.</li>
<li>&quot;SCP-3178 consumers lose the part of the brain&quot; feels weird. Does that part just cease to exist? It might make more sense to say that it deteriorates</li>
<li>SCP-3178-1 feel really disconnected from the rest of the SCP. I'd either remove them or find a way to more smoothly incorporate them.</li>
<li>Test logs are good, but a couple of them seem a bit repetitive, maybe remove a couple</li>
</ul>
<p>On the whole, I think the concept definitely has potential, but there are too many issues for me to give it a +1, so I'm going to make it a non-vote.</p>

