<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong>Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong>SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong>SCP-XXXX is a wormhole of anomalous nature located on a deep-sea level, it has the appearance of a 2&#160;km deep round trench. Any organism or structure that trespasses it fully will shrink down to a 0.001% of its original size. Set hole will unexplainably start to inhale during 2-3 hours specially during June, July and August.</p>
<p>This wormhole is connected to SCP-XXXX-A, (a standard plastic family pool) which is property of a Caucasian family located in ████████████████. After diving 1&#160;km into the pit 1&#160;km, the walls will start to resemble the tube of a filter pump. Once entering SCP-XXXX-A through the filter hole, it appears to have a size of 2000km long, 1500km wide and 1000km high from set perspective.</p>
<p>SCP-XXXX-A possesses a thin plastic layer partially covering the surface, aswell as many human and insect organic tissues of massive size floating at the surface or underwater, and a chlorine dispenser originally used as a safe base to monitor the surroundings.</p>
<p>There are 5 inhabitants in SCP-XXXX, labeled SCP-XXXX-1 through 5. These are 4 caucasian human individuals (2 male and 2 female) and a canine creature (from the <em>Canis lupus familiaris</em> race). These entities only appear during certain daytime hours in the summer season, and communication with these individuals at first was impossible and dangerous.</p>
<p>The wormhole's origin was later discovered by reaching the surface and achieving connection. The foundation sent a team towards the location and acquired the anomaly, as well as capturing the family to interview them about the item. The pool was brought into a containment cell and since then it has been studied its size-shifting properties.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong>During the first encounter with the wormhole, the foundation sent multiple teams to enter SCP-XXXX. Once arriving to the other end, they were amazed at the ocean despite being empty and confusing. Other than that, no other anomalies were present until the appearance of SCP-XXXX-1 to 5, which were a threat to the team since the entities weren't aware of them, causing many casualties. After receiving information about the location of SCP-XXXX,it was successfully contained.</p>
<p><strong>Hook-Attention-Grabber:</strong>This anomaly is simple, a wormhole that connects the ocean to a pool. However, the most interesting part is the many changes this SCP goes through the more understood it is, until completely containing it. If done correctly, it should be classified as a Euclid, then reclassified Keter, and finally Safe.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong>This SCP has a lot of layers and changes. It may be a bit confusing due to everything it presents so i'll need to do it correctly. I'm fairly new here so I understand if there are problems with the idea, so please tell me since i want to improve on this concept.</p>

